════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
 48l — the cost of the list<(atom, term)> workaround
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

─── §1  A MISSPELLED KEY, and §2 a wrong value type ───
  Correct      42
  Typo         0
  WrongType    "unset"

  ✓ the typo is SILENT: compiles clean, runs clean, returns the absent answer.
    Indistinguishable from a legitimately absent optional key.

  ✓ CONTROL: a bare `term` reaching an `int` parameter is a COMPILE ERROR.
    So the VALUE domain is checked — the checker forces a narrowing, and
    WrongType above fails as a value at run time rather than silently.
    The blindness is the KEY domain specifically, not "everything is term".

─── §3  CAN A CLAUSE HEAD ASK THE KEY QUESTION? ───
  user_id written first        :saw_user
  locale written first         :no_user

  ✓ Same key set. Different write order. Different answer. Both compile clean.
    The head cannot express "does this channel carry key K", so key
    dispatch must move into the body — which is what B#'s whole dispatch
    story exists to avoid.

─── §4  CONTROL — the checker on a CLOSED key set ───
  (this control routes through a record: an anonymous brace map cannot be
   CONSTRUCTED — there is no bare-brace expression production, 48j wall two.)
  closed union, both arms            :is_admin
  union grew by one member           REFUSED — not exhaustive

  ✓ Over a CLOSED key set the guarantee is live: add a member and the
    clause set goes red. The engine works. §1 and §3 are not the engine
    being weak — they are the open key domain being outside its reach.

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
 The trade, in one line:

   The unchecked open key domain EXISTS TODAY, spelled as a list.
   Adding map<K,V> does not create it — it makes it a type the
   compiler knows the shape of. Exhaustiveness over open keys is
   vacuous either way; §4 shows what is NOT being given up.
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
